      "message": "On Unix systems, `std::fs::write` overwrites the file content but preserves existing permissions. \n\nIf a rule author temporarily sets `is_executable \u003d True`, builds, and then reverts it to `False` (or removes the argument), the file will remain executable on disk. This can lead to non-deterministic build results between local environments and CI.\n\nTo ensure idempotent builds, consider setting the permissions explicitly regardless of the `is_executable` flag (e.g., `0o755` if `True`, and `0o644` if `False`).",
